WEBVTT

00:01:20.848 --> 00:01:24.051
< What, no greeting? I've been waiting for you. >

00:01:24.051 --> 00:01:25.746
< Tonight's busy for me. >

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:28.848
< You noticed we were following you? >

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:31.859
< To get right down to it,
I've been the one scouting YOU. >

00:01:31.859 --> 00:01:35.420
<i></i>

00:01:35.796 --> 00:01:39.596
< Who are you? An agent
from the Japanese army? >

00:01:40.167 --> 00:01:42.431
< Yeah. That's about right. >

00:01:42.903 --> 00:01:47.306
< I've been on you because I know
you're with the local warlord, Zong-Wu Liu. >

00:01:48.042 --> 00:01:51.445
< Hold on. This is actually
one big miscalculation. >

00:01:51.445 --> 00:01:54.548
< It looks like you've only undertaken
the procurement of military goods. >

00:01:54.548 --> 00:01:57.278
< You're one of Liu's business partners, huh? >

00:01:58.485 --> 00:02:01.555
< I'm investigating the kidnapping of
the head of the Kaburagi Conglomerate. >

00:02:01.555 --> 00:02:07.895
< If you're not involved with that,
I'm not interested in ya. >

00:02:07.895 --> 00:02:10.197
< Don't you go following me anymore, either. >

00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:14.668
< You all are trying to stamp out our activities! >

00:02:14.668 --> 00:02:17.296
< Hey, hold on. You've got the wrong idea. >

00:02:37.357 --> 00:02:43.130
<Sorry. It's hard to hold back
when it's sudden like that. >

00:02:43.130 --> 00:02:45.199
< Wh-what are you? >

00:02:45.199 --> 00:02:50.571
< I'm curious about you again.
About WHY you had the wrong idea. >

00:02:50.571 --> 00:02:53.173
< Feel like talking for a little bit? >

00:02:53.173 --> 00:02:55.164
< Y-yes. >

00:03:04.518 --> 00:03:08.477
Shangha i - 1931

00:03:09.723 --> 00:03:13.682
-NIGHT RAID-

00:03:23.103 --> 00:03:24.832
Shanghai.

00:03:25.172 --> 00:03:29.302
The foreign-controlled area known as
"the Settlement" continues to expand.

00:03:30.077 --> 00:03:35.606
A congested city, where funds pouring in from
Western powers lead to accelerated growth.

00:03:36.583 --> 00:03:45.651
Conglomerates, soldiers, artists, criminals,
refugees, revolutionaries, and spies...

00:03:49.062 --> 00:03:53.499
On these streets, people from different
countries, different walks of life

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:55.795
come together and are intermingled.

00:04:02.743 --> 00:04:07.646
It's a foreign country within China,
where dreams collide with nightmares.

00:04:07.748 --> 00:04:09.113
That is Shanghai.

00:04:12.352 --> 00:04:15.321
<i></i>

00:04:20.761 --> 00:04:24.219
Some people call this "The Devil's City".

00:04:30.637 --> 00:04:32.798
I can't confirm from here.

00:04:40.781 --> 00:04:45.548
Four military policemen are approaching.
They came in through the west entrance.

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:51.186
No sudden moves. Isn't he here yet? Aoi.

00:04:56.630 --> 00:04:57.995
One of them was shot.

00:04:58.599 --> 00:05:00.032
Here they come.

00:05:11.211 --> 00:05:12.746
What of Mr. Kaburagi?

00:05:12.746 --> 00:05:14.611
I only saw from behind.

00:05:16.216 --> 00:05:17.114
Let's go!

00:05:46.647 --> 00:05:47.414
Can you see anything?

00:05:47.414 --> 00:05:49.075
Go straight, to Suzhou Bay.

00:06:02.996 --> 00:06:04.930
Wait! Don't rush off!

00:06:05.432 --> 00:06:06.558
It's dangerous!

00:06:24.785 --> 00:06:25.819
Are you all right?

00:06:25.819 --> 00:06:26.877
Yes.

00:06:31.358 --> 00:06:32.416
Aoi?

00:07:07.527 --> 00:07:08.892
< He's a tough one. >

00:07:30.417 --> 00:07:31.816
< Why you! >

00:07:33.153 --> 00:07:34.245
The hostage!

00:07:36.423 --> 00:07:37.617
You all right?

00:08:08.455 --> 00:08:11.515
They got us. This isn't Mr. Kaburagi.

00:08:13.326 --> 00:08:14.691
A decoy?

00:08:16.329 --> 00:08:17.990
I was just about out of time.

00:08:18.598 --> 00:08:22.402
Why do you not act as planned?

00:08:22.402 --> 00:08:24.871
It hit me they could use the river to get away.

00:08:24.871 --> 00:08:28.238
So you merely acted
according to your own whim?

00:08:28.442 --> 00:08:30.377
Try knowing the situation first.

00:08:30.377 --> 00:08:35.610
I reconsidered the situation.
My aim wasn't too far off, either.

00:08:36.049 --> 00:08:39.746
Still, the enemy got the better of us this time.

00:08:43.490 --> 00:08:46.493
Why didn't you use it?

00:08:46.493 --> 00:08:48.791
Things got a little dangerous.

00:08:50.063 --> 00:08:52.299
I use it if I have to.

00:08:52.299 --> 00:08:54.096
That's all there is to it.

00:09:04.611 --> 00:09:07.705
It seems things got rather out of hand. Even you.

00:09:08.181 --> 00:09:12.675
We didn't expect the military police
to storm where he was being held.

00:09:13.019 --> 00:09:18.058
The bonds of trust have yet to be established.

00:09:18.058 --> 00:09:20.393
Between the higher-ups and us...

00:09:20.393 --> 00:09:24.887
And perhaps between you all as well.

00:09:27.267 --> 00:09:32.261
In any case... Yukina, have you gotten
anything out of the three decoys?

00:09:33.139 --> 00:09:35.403
Piecing together the information
I could read off them...

00:09:38.712 --> 00:09:40.543
Mr. Kaburagi was...

00:09:41.147 --> 00:09:44.639
transported to the headquarters
of Zong-Wu Liu's army.

00:09:44.751 --> 00:09:45.785
Their headquarters?

00:09:45.785 --> 00:09:48.622
They fled after losing last month's conflict,

00:09:48.622 --> 00:09:51.955
and not even the Nationalist Party
knows where their main forces are.

00:09:52.192 --> 00:09:55.923
You're saying you know
where they've mobilized?

00:09:56.429 --> 00:10:00.033
It's not clear whether it's their "main forces",

00:10:00.033 --> 00:10:05.403
but they've come together at an old fort
on the banks of a river east of Nanking.

00:10:05.639 --> 00:10:08.141
Those three are just grunts.

00:10:08.141 --> 00:10:10.837
I bet they haven't been given any real info.

00:10:12.412 --> 00:10:15.575
We'll watch over those three.

00:10:18.118 --> 00:10:21.488
We took an airplane for a peek over there earlier.

00:10:21.488 --> 00:10:25.083
Natsume says he confirmed Kaburagi is there.

00:10:27.627 --> 00:10:32.799
Actually, via a negotiator,
their demands have changed.

00:10:32.799 --> 00:10:34.027
Changed?

00:10:34.234 --> 00:10:39.439
So their demand that the Japanese military
surrender all their weapons...

00:10:39.439 --> 00:10:42.909
...is no more. Now they want money.

00:10:42.909 --> 00:10:46.112
Yeah, well, that's a pretty obvious one.

00:10:46.112 --> 00:10:48.046
But why now?

00:10:48.214 --> 00:10:50.083
They kidnapped Mr. Kaburagi

00:10:50.083 --> 00:10:55.885
so they could procure weapons capable
of fighting back against the Nationalist Party.

00:10:56.122 --> 00:10:58.792
They've tried not to reveal
the weakness of their military,

00:10:58.792 --> 00:11:05.561
but they're armed with old, cheap weaponry,
holdovers from the Mexican Revolution.

00:11:05.799 --> 00:11:10.293
They stand no chance against the latest German
weaponry owned by the Nationalist Party.

00:11:11.204 --> 00:11:18.235
They grew impatient because the Japanese
wouldn't hand over their weapons?

00:11:18.345 --> 00:11:24.351
But they don't have time to wait while
they trade money for weapons, do they?

00:11:24.351 --> 00:11:30.085
They don't have the means to get weapons
from Europe or America that quickly.

00:11:30.357 --> 00:11:32.917
Indeed. That's how things stand.

00:11:33.460 --> 00:11:35.662
That's how they stand, huh?

00:11:35.662 --> 00:11:38.932
They're demanding the ransom money
not from the Kaburagi Conglomerate

00:11:38.932 --> 00:11:41.765
but from the Japanese government.

00:11:42.736 --> 00:11:44.033
Impossible!

00:11:46.773 --> 00:11:49.071
This has gotten kinda troublesome...

00:11:49.809 --> 00:11:54.041
How so? Bringing back Kaburagi
will be the end of it.

00:11:54.881 --> 00:11:59.511
Oh, the military policeman shot
last night seems to have died.

00:11:59.986 --> 00:12:03.217
You all be sure to take care of yourselves.

00:12:03.623 --> 00:12:06.259
This first job may have thinned out the ranks,

00:12:06.259 --> 00:12:08.693
but what lies ahead will be difficult.

00:12:17.404 --> 00:12:19.201
What kind of fighting force do they have?

00:12:19.305 --> 00:12:20.670
About 2,000 guys.

00:12:20.774 --> 00:12:22.605
A whole squadron, huh?

00:12:22.709 --> 00:12:25.542
They're probably hiding
in the surrounding forest, too.

00:12:25.879 --> 00:12:28.313
Natsume, what's this line?

00:12:28.415 --> 00:12:29.939
An underground escape route.

00:12:30.050 --> 00:12:32.848
It's old, but it's reinforced with rock
and hasn't caved in.

00:12:32.952 --> 00:12:35.887
You should've mentioned that sooner!
Talk about a gift horse.

00:12:35.989 --> 00:12:37.217
It's no good.

00:12:37.323 --> 00:12:40.622
The military is using this building,
the exit from which faces the fort.

00:12:40.694 --> 00:12:41.428
2nd floor (Kaburagi
Two watching the stairs

00:12:41.428 --> 00:12:45.665
2nd floor (Kaburagi
Two watching the stairs
Also, it's quite far from the tower
where Kaburagi is being held.

00:12:45.665 --> 00:12:48.225
2nd floor (Kaburagi
Two watching the stairs
There's a way to get around that...

00:13:02.649 --> 00:13:04.084
< Where'd it come from? >

00:13:04.084 --> 00:13:05.312
<i></i>

00:13:34.180 --> 00:13:36.483
< From the forest across the way? >

00:13:36.483 --> 00:13:40.943
<i></i>

00:13:41.454 --> 00:13:45.083
< It's probably a hunter.
He's not aiming at us here. >

00:14:25.198 --> 00:14:26.927
Sure is dark outside.

00:14:27.233 --> 00:14:30.430
A moonlit night. Your eyes will adjust soon.

00:14:31.805 --> 00:14:34.205
Yeah. I can see.

00:14:34.507 --> 00:14:38.534
There's a novel I think of every time
I look down from up high.

00:14:38.778 --> 00:14:41.804
Especially when flying at night above a city.

00:14:42.048 --> 00:14:43.817
By Saint-Exupéry?

00:14:43.817 --> 00:14:45.751
"Watcher in the Attic."

00:14:46.119 --> 00:14:50.078
Edogawa Rampo? That's a rather high attic.

00:14:50.824 --> 00:14:52.689
I never thought YOU read Rampo.

00:14:53.193 --> 00:14:54.785
I hate him.

00:14:55.395 --> 00:14:57.530
He's interesting.

00:14:57.530 --> 00:15:01.864
That attic is like our powers, don't you think?

00:15:02.802 --> 00:15:04.599
What do you mean?

00:15:04.971 --> 00:15:08.998
When that man in the apartment attic
would look down into the rooms,

00:15:09.108 --> 00:15:12.512
he'd feel ecstasy at the sense of superiority
over the other tenants.

00:15:12.512 --> 00:15:13.672
Ah.

00:15:14.247 --> 00:15:17.978
What makes people so happy at having
an advantage over their opponent?

00:15:18.184 --> 00:15:21.085
Winning through an even fight
should have that much more meaning.

00:15:21.454 --> 00:15:25.049
Don't tell me that's why
you don't use your power!

00:15:26.359 --> 00:15:27.861
You're serious?

00:15:27.861 --> 00:15:31.058
I don't place my comrades' lives on the line.

00:15:31.798 --> 00:15:37.327
I use it if I have to. But it's not
as handy as you seem to think.

00:15:51.517 --> 00:15:52.575
Show me.

00:16:28.187 --> 00:16:31.424
< Watermelons are in season,
so we could get some. >

00:16:31.424 --> 00:16:33.221
< After all, we were partners. >

00:16:44.971 --> 00:16:47.006
< And what happened then? >

00:16:47.006 --> 00:16:49.809
<i></i>

00:16:49.809 --> 00:16:51.504
Left at the next corner.

00:16:51.611 --> 00:16:54.011
Once you turn, it will be the building on the right.

00:16:54.113 --> 00:16:56.673
Yes, that one. The second floor.

00:16:57.150 --> 00:16:59.252
< Well, what do you say to that? >

00:16:59.252 --> 00:17:00.446
< Ah... >

00:17:02.588 --> 00:17:04.357
< Has our guest been playing nice? >

00:17:04.357 --> 00:17:05.258
< Yeah. >

00:17:05.258 --> 00:17:07.226
< What kind of food does the guest eat? >

00:17:07.226 --> 00:17:09.421
< Don't look. That would piss me off. >

00:17:21.274 --> 00:17:23.710
Mr. Kaburagi, correct?

00:17:23.710 --> 00:17:25.610
We're special agents.

00:17:27.213 --> 00:17:31.513
We've come to get you, but...
you seem oddly at home.

00:17:31.751 --> 00:17:35.346
Y-yes. They've been unexpectedly kind.

00:17:36.022 --> 00:17:37.390
I knew it.

00:17:37.390 --> 00:17:39.085
You made a deal with Liu.

00:17:39.993 --> 00:17:42.695
I was threatened, and had no choice.

00:17:42.695 --> 00:17:46.766
You suggested they buy weapons with the
ransom money paid out by the government.

00:17:46.766 --> 00:17:50.603
It can't be helped, so long as the army
refuses to hand over its weapons.

00:17:50.603 --> 00:17:52.070
But that's not all, is it?

00:17:52.372 --> 00:17:56.536
You arranged for your company to handle
procuring the weapons, didn't you?

00:17:59.012 --> 00:18:01.748
You used this opportunity to do some business?

00:18:01.748 --> 00:18:05.775
You've got guys who are ticked off
at being cut out of a major deal like this.

00:18:06.919 --> 00:18:09.956
It's just a matter of time
before this faction is no more.

00:18:09.956 --> 00:18:12.186
That much is obvious.

00:18:12.425 --> 00:18:16.555
If you give them new weaponry,
it will just prolong this futile conflict.

00:18:18.031 --> 00:18:19.332
What are you?

00:18:19.332 --> 00:18:20.799
We need you to sleep for a bit.

00:18:27.473 --> 00:18:29.031
< What was that sound just now? >

00:18:29.175 --> 00:18:30.267
< Running. >

00:18:34.047 --> 00:18:34.847
< What happened? >

00:18:34.847 --> 00:18:37.483
<i></i>

00:18:37.483 --> 00:18:38.818
< A sudden illness? >

00:18:38.818 --> 00:18:41.218
< In any case, we're taking him to the medic. >

00:18:45.124 --> 00:18:47.649
The real food detail is getting closer.

00:18:48.227 --> 00:18:49.785
Isn't there something you can do?

00:18:49.896 --> 00:18:51.830
If you reach the castle walls...

00:18:51.931 --> 00:18:53.421
Oh, no.

00:18:57.570 --> 00:19:01.074
Getting caught was part of the plan,
but not this fast!

00:19:01.074 --> 00:19:02.336
Cut the chatter.

00:19:03.943 --> 00:19:06.935
That way's dangerous.
Detour around the west bank.

00:19:08.214 --> 00:19:10.273
Stop! Wait there a minute.

00:19:17.423 --> 00:19:18.185
Not yet!

00:19:29.302 --> 00:19:30.735
Dammit!

00:19:31.003 --> 00:19:35.133
I've used a lot of time.
I might be out when it counts.

00:19:35.508 --> 00:19:39.342
Could it be you rely on your power too much,
and haven't learned restraint?

00:19:40.113 --> 00:19:41.705
Let's move.

00:19:46.953 --> 00:19:49.055
< Run! Get in formation! >

00:19:49.055 --> 00:19:52.959
The last squad has just moved out.
There's no one inside right now.

00:19:52.959 --> 00:19:53.593
You wanna do it?

00:19:53.593 --> 00:19:57.196
Let's wait a little. That squad
should move farther away.

00:19:57.196 --> 00:19:59.824
Oh, no. Someone's coming from the south.

00:20:00.166 --> 00:20:02.225
There are... six of them.

00:20:02.735 --> 00:20:05.104
I've got about two minutes left.

00:20:05.104 --> 00:20:06.806
All right, let's go.

00:20:06.806 --> 00:20:07.773
Yeah.

00:20:07.773 --> 00:20:08.330
Yukina.

00:20:08.441 --> 00:20:09.601
I heard.

00:20:09.909 --> 00:20:11.342
Let's get started.

00:20:11.511 --> 00:20:12.478
Natsume.

00:20:20.887 --> 00:20:22.286
< Take emergency positions! >

00:20:22.455 --> 00:20:25.219
90 seconds, 89, 88...

00:20:25.324 --> 00:20:26.256
87...

00:20:32.165 --> 00:20:33.132
< Hey! >

00:20:35.535 --> 00:20:36.627
< There they are! >

00:20:42.909 --> 00:20:45.537
< You'll hit the hostage!
Don't shoot! Capture them! >

00:20:59.358 --> 00:21:00.256
60 seconds...

00:21:07.934 --> 00:21:09.094
30 seconds left.

00:21:09.268 --> 00:21:10.166
Look out!

00:21:26.052 --> 00:21:27.610
I'm out of time!

00:21:29.422 --> 00:21:31.014
Oh! Zero seconds left!

00:21:31.123 --> 00:21:32.112
A little late there.

00:21:33.426 --> 00:21:35.394
Yukina, where's that way out?

00:21:42.868 --> 00:21:43.836
What's that?

00:21:43.836 --> 00:21:45.201
A real barrage.

00:21:45.638 --> 00:21:47.765
< An enemy raid! Enemy raid! >

00:21:51.877 --> 00:21:52.844
That's...

00:21:57.683 --> 00:21:59.275
The Naval Jack of the Republic of China!

00:22:00.019 --> 00:22:01.281
The Nationalist Party, huh?

00:22:01.621 --> 00:22:04.385
So the Nationalist Party
has sniffed out Liu's army?

00:22:06.892 --> 00:22:08.223
I guess.

00:22:11.297 --> 00:22:12.696
You're both all right, aren't you?

00:22:12.798 --> 00:22:13.787
You're unharmed?

00:22:13.966 --> 00:22:16.434
Yeah. But what about that way out?

00:22:17.003 --> 00:22:18.197
Well...

00:22:18.304 --> 00:22:21.637
One of the blasts leveled the entrance.
It's unusable.

00:22:23.342 --> 00:22:24.434
What?

00:22:26.479 --> 00:22:27.673
Damn!

00:22:28.347 --> 00:22:29.507
Kazura...

00:22:30.683 --> 00:22:32.742
It's time for you to use your power, right?

00:22:34.720 --> 00:22:38.891
I don't know what your problem is,
but you should relax.

00:22:38.891 --> 00:22:44.488
Your past or silly pride or whatever
has nothing to do with us now. Right?

00:22:44.597 --> 00:22:45.529
But...

00:22:47.166 --> 00:22:49.031
You're needed now.

00:22:54.740 --> 00:22:55.502
All right.

00:22:56.776 --> 00:23:00.177
Yukina, I'd like something to focus my will on.

00:23:00.279 --> 00:23:02.008
Okay. A light, right?

00:23:03.282 --> 00:23:04.715
I'll be back.

00:23:08.154 --> 00:23:09.178
Madam!

00:23:10.489 --> 00:23:11.786
I'm all right.

00:23:20.833 --> 00:23:21.901
What gives?

00:23:21.901 --> 00:23:23.027
We're going.

00:23:50.296 --> 00:23:52.321
Yahoo!

00:23:56.469 --> 00:23:58.528
That was just like aerobatics!

00:24:00.873 --> 00:24:04.331
Calm yourself. It's not as useful as you'd think.

00:24:05.845 --> 00:24:07.613
You finally used it!

00:24:07.613 --> 00:24:12.073
I used it because it was necessary.
That's all there is to it.

00:24:28.801 --> 00:24:32.328
You gave the Nationalist Party a bit of intel
about Liu's faction, didn't you?

00:24:32.772 --> 00:24:37.038
Because Liu is a nuisance to the Party as well.

00:24:37.209 --> 00:24:41.305
It's easiest to attack from both sides,
inside and out.

00:24:41.714 --> 00:24:46.617
How kind. The Nationalist Party and Japan
have a strained relationship.

00:24:47.119 --> 00:24:49.221
I haven't violated any national policies.

00:24:49.221 --> 00:24:52.156
Prosperity and stability throughout
East Asia is the ideal.

00:24:53.826 --> 00:24:57.785
You don't plan to get rid of those
who witnessed us, do you?

00:25:00.833 --> 00:25:03.996
You're quite observant. As I'd hoped.

00:25:04.637 --> 00:25:07.873
The power you all possess
is itself a military secret.

00:25:07.873 --> 00:25:10.176
Not all those who witnessed it have to die,

00:25:10.176 --> 00:25:13.737
but reducing the chance of that secret leaking,
even a little, is worth it.

00:25:14.346 --> 00:25:16.280
Don't get so worked up.

00:25:17.383 --> 00:25:20.045
What happened can't be helped.

00:25:20.886 --> 00:25:26.358
They may be a rural faction,
but there's no telling where soldiers may die.

00:25:26.358 --> 00:25:29.327
The same goes for you all. And me.

00:25:29.462 --> 00:25:31.487
Don't you think?

00:25:31.697 --> 00:25:36.691
Still, this has shown the higher-ups your worth.

00:25:37.036 --> 00:25:42.174
A win-win situation.
This has become an excellent pretext...

00:25:42.174 --> 00:25:44.443
for the higher-ups, the Nationalist Party,

00:25:44.443 --> 00:25:47.446
and for us, the Sakurai Agency as well.

00:25:47.446 --> 00:25:49.209
There's another gain.

00:25:51.417 --> 00:25:52.751
Well...

00:25:52.751 --> 00:25:56.243
This fell out of Kaburagi's jacket pocket.

00:25:56.589 --> 00:26:00.457
It looks like the weapon order that Liu
placed to the Kaburagi Conglomerate.

00:26:00.860 --> 00:26:05.030
I see. This could be rather useful.

00:26:05.030 --> 00:26:08.701
But what made you want to give this to me?

00:26:08.701 --> 00:26:14.006
Kaburagi sold weapons to both enemies
and allies, and that pissed me off.

00:26:14.006 --> 00:26:15.473
More than you.

00:26:25.484 --> 00:26:29.443
I wouldn't want you to hate me
more than you do.

00:26:35.027 --> 00:26:37.461
All these guys are hard to deal with.

00:26:38.097 --> 00:26:41.294
This sure is the "Devil's City".

00:26:47.506 --> 00:26:52.307
Episode 1
The Rescue

00:26:52.611 --> 00:26:59.351
Bokura sora takaku kimi wo mamotteku

00:26:59.351 --> 00:27:06.348
Tsuyosa hakanasa no kono hane de

00:27:13.165 --> 00:27:20.039
Nukumori wo oshiete kureta

00:27:20.039 --> 00:27:26.911
Kanashimi wo nugutte kureta

00:27:27.212 --> 00:27:33.052
Koko kara asu e yukou, zutto kimi no soba de

00:27:33.052 --> 00:27:38.957
Koko kara asu e yukou, zutto kimi no soba de

00:27:39.925 --> 00:27:53.505
Ano hi boku ga mune ni chikatta yakusoku sa

00:27:53.505 --> 00:28:01.113
Ima bokura sora takaku kimi wo mamotteku

00:28:01.113 --> 00:28:08.087
Tsuyosa hakanasa no kono hane de

00:28:08.087 --> 00:28:14.890
Kimi no nakigao mo, kanashimi no yoake mo

00:28:15.260 --> 00:28:21.221
Mou mitaku wa nai kara

00:28:24.703 --> 00:28:29.538
A tone that can be played scatters
fragments of the past in one's heart.

00:28:30.209 --> 00:28:33.110
A violinist believed to be a spy.

00:28:33.646 --> 00:28:36.949
A finger controlling the modulation of sound,

00:28:36.949 --> 00:28:39.543
and a finger that probes the darkness
of chaos and confusion.

00:28:40.219 --> 00:28:42.517
No undue force was required.

00:28:43.589 --> 00:28:47.047
He only wished to love music...

